{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long double dbl;\nconst int MAXM = 1 << 20;\nconst double EPS = 1E-9;\n\nstruct Val {\n    dbl coeff, cnst;\n    Val(dbl c = 0.0L, dbl k = 0.0L) : coeff(c), cnst(k) {}\n};\n\ntypedef array<Val, MAXM> DpArray;\nstatic DpArray dp;\n\nint n, k;\ndouble prob[25];\n\ndouble Solve(int victim) {\n    if (prob[victim] < EPS) return 0.0;\n\n    dp.fill(Val());\n    dp[0] = Val(1.0L, 0.0L);\n\n    int total = 1 << n;\n    int vbit = 1 << victim;\n\n    for (int mask = 1; mask < total; ++mask) {\n        if (mask & vbit) continue;\n\n        Val cur(0.0L, 0.0L);\n        dbl same = 0.0L;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            if (i == victim) continue;\n            if (mask & (1 << i)) {\n                same += prob[i];\n                const Val& prev = dp[mask ^ (1 << i)];\n                cur.coeff += prev.coeff * prob[i];\n                cur.cnst += prev.cnst * prob[i];\n            }\n        }\n\n        dp[mask].coeff = cur.coeff / (1.0L - same);\n        dp[mask].cnst = cur.cnst / (1.0L - same);\n    }\n\n    Val totalVal(1.0L, 0.0L);\n    for (int mask = 1; mask < total; ++mask) {\n        if (!(mask & vbit)) {\n            totalVal.coeff += dp[mask].coeff;\n            totalVal.cnst += dp[mask].cnst;\n        }\n    }\n\n    dbl alpha = (1.0L - totalVal.cnst) / totalVal.coeff;\n\n    Val badVal(0.0L, 0.0L);\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < total; ++mask) {\n        if (!(mask & vbit) && __builtin_popcount(mask) >= k) {\n            badVal.coeff += dp[mask].coeff;\n            badVal.cnst += dp[mask].cnst;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return (double)(1.0L - (alpha * badVal.coeff + badVal.cnst));\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d%d\", &n, &k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) scanf(\"%lf\", &prob[i]);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (i) putchar(' ');\n        printf(\"%.12f\", Solve(i));\n    }\n    putchar('\\n');\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\nMAXM = 1 << 20\nEPS = 1e-9\n\ndef Solve(victim, n, k, prob):\n    if prob[victim] < EPS:\n        return 0.0\n\n    total = 1 << n\n    vbit = 1 << victim\n\n    coeff = [0.0] * total\n    cnst = [0.0] * total\n    coeff[0] = 1.0\n    cnst[0] = 0.0\n\n    for mask in range(1, total):\n        if mask & vbit:\n            continue\n\n        cur_coeff = 0.0\n        cur_cnst = 0.0\n        same = 0.0\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            if i == victim:\n                continue\n            if mask & (1 << i):\n                same += prob[i]\n                prev_mask = mask ^ (1 << i)\n                cur_coeff += coeff[prev_mask] * prob[i]\n                cur_cnst += cnst[prev_mask] * prob[i]\n\n        coeff[mask] = cur_coeff / (1.0 - same)\n        cnst[mask] = cur_cnst / (1.0 - same)\n\n    total_coeff = 1.0\n    total_cnst = 0.0\n    for mask in range(1, total):\n        if not (mask & vbit):\n            total_coeff += coeff[mask]\n            total_cnst += cnst[mask]\n\n    alpha = (1.0 - total_cnst) / total_coeff\n\n    bad_coeff = 0.0\n    bad_cnst = 0.0\n    for mask in range(total):\n        if not (mask & vbit) and mask.bit_count() >= k:\n            bad_coeff += coeff[mask]\n            bad_cnst += cnst[mask]\n\n    return 1.0 - (alpha * bad_coeff + bad_cnst)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    k = int(next(it))\n    prob = [float(next(it)) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    results = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        results.append(\"{:.12f}\".format(Solve(i, n, k, prob)))\n    sys.stdout.write(\" \".join(results) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00018165845540352166, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00014423283573705703, -0.002518222201615572, -9.60780744208023e-05, -0.3134816884994507, -0.062139254063367844, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.00016640232934150845, -0.7588273882865906, -0.00011896379146492109, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0005489272880367935, -5.722029527532868e-06, -4.291525328881107e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.029771246016025543, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.401333666872233e-05, -0.000987876090221107, -0.00011336160969221964, -0.5765014886856079, -0.0019317077239975333, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0509633831679821, -0.25310978293418884, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.01816236972808838, 0.0, -1.3232143828645349e-05, -6.139089964563027e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.001312824198976159, -5.125986263010418e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.030173959210515022, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.007255159318447113, -9.53673